::SPEECH_U04_L03_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U04_L03_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.RES.03
Question:
Source: Short planned movement breaks may help students return to study with better focus. Which paraphrase is most accurate?
{
~A. Use the source to prove something it never says#This answer shows a misconception. Return to the source details and check whether the choice supports accurate research-based speaking.
=B. Brief planned movement breaks can support focus without replacing study time#Correct. This answer uses the source accurately and connects the information to research-supported speech communication.
~C. Choose a detail because it sounds impressive#This answer may mention the topic, but it does not show the careful reading or reasoning required for source use.
~D. Ignore limits that are written in the source#This answer weakens communication by relying on a surface detail instead of accurate source comprehension.
}
::SPEECH_U04_L03_GuidedPractice_Q02::
